      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JWKS Availability",
      "description": "Also aggregated with min. Alert on this rather than on a probe: reaching the JWKS is deliberately not a health check, because a 503 on /health restarts the pod and an unready pod leaves the Service, which would take the scheduler down over a dependency cron does not use.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "area"
            }
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "min(auth_jwks_available{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"})",
          "legendFormat": "available"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pods Serving the API vs Pods Up",
      "description": "The two lines diverging is the case a single gauge hides: pods running and scraped, but not all of them serving the UI. Since api_enabled is decided once at startup from configuration, a gap that appears after a rollout means the new pods came up with different configuration from the old ones.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(api_enabled{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"})",
          "legendFormat": "serving the API"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(up{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"})",
          "legendFormat": "pods up"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 250,
      "title": "Connect API — Requests",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request Rate by Route",
      "description": "One series per RPC. The route label is the Connect procedure path and carries no identifiers, so this cannot fan out with traffic — the series count is the number of RPCs in the proto. OPTIONS preflights appear here too, because the middleware wraps outside the CORS handler on purpose: a preflight rejected for a missing allowed header breaks every browser call before it reaches a handler, and instrumented inside the wrapper that outage would leave no trace at all.\n\nOPTIONS is excluded so this counts RPCs rather than round trips: under cross-origin use a browser sends a preflight and then the real call, which would read as double the true rate. Preflights are still counted, and are visible on Request Rate by Status as 204 when allowed and 405 when refused — 405s on a route are the CORS signal to watch, not a general non-2xx rate.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (route) (rate(http_requests_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", method!=\"OPTIONS\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request Rate by Status",
      "description": "Non-2xx here is the UI being refused. Cross-read it against JWKS Availability above: a wall of 401s with that gauge at 0 is a JWT authority outage rather than bad callers.\n\nThis panel keeps OPTIONS, unlike the rate-by-route and latency panels beside it. That is where preflights belong: 204 is an allowed one, 405 is a refused one, and a rising 405 line against a route means browsers are being turned away before they reach a handler.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 15
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 52,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Trustworthy percentiles, which is not automatic: pipeline-lib applies no bucket boundaries for you, and its fallback is the OTel SDK ladder tuned for milliseconds. Against a seconds unit every real request would land in one bucket and every percentile would be interpolation noise. The service passes SubsecondLatencyBuckets explicitly, so the ladder runs 0.005s to 10s.\n\nOne failure these cannot show: a request that never completes is never observed, because the histogram records on return. Nothing on this board would move — not the percentiles, not the error ratio, since no status is ever written. http_active_requests is where a hung request shows, as a gauge that climbs and does not come back down; it has no panel because at this traffic shape its correct value is 0 and a graph of a constant is not worth a slot. Query it directly if requests are disappearing rather than failing.\n\nOPTIONS is excluded. A CORS preflight is instrumented deliberately — a refused one is a 405 and is how a cross-origin outage becomes visible — but an allowed one is a near-zero 204 sharing this route label, which would drag the percentile down towards it. It does not arise in the deployed configuration, where the UI is same-origin through the Kong prefix and no preflight is sent.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 15
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", method!=\"OPTIONS\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", method!=\"OPTIONS\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", method!=\"OPTIONS\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 53,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration p95 by Route",
      "description": "Which RPC is slow. The write paths go through Postgres and, for a firing, the job engine as well, so RunJobNow and StartScan sit on a different timescale from a list call and should not be read against one another.\n\nOPTIONS is excluded. A CORS preflight is instrumented deliberately — a refused one is a 405 and is how a cross-origin outage becomes visible — but an allowed one is a near-zero 204 sharing this route label, which would drag the percentile down towards it. It does not arise in the deployed configuration, where the UI is same-origin through the Kong prefix and no preflight is sent.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, route) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", method!=\"OPTIONS\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 54,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error Ratio (non-2xx)",
      "description": "Share of requests answered outside 2xx. clamp_min keeps the ratio defined while the API is idle rather than returning NaN.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.05
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_requests_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", status!~\"2..\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(http_requests_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "error ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 56,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Payload Size p95",
      "description": "Both percentiles are trustworthy, on deliberately different ladders. Response size uses BodySizeBuckets (256B to 4MB) because a ListRuns page is measured in kilobytes. Request size keeps the SDK default, which resolves 0 to 10000 bytes with seven boundaries below 256 — the right ladder for the small Connect messages this API accepts, where BodySizeBuckets would collapse every one of them into its first bucket.\n\nWatch the request-size ceiling: above 10000 bytes everything piles into +Inf and that percentile saturates. scan_config is arbitrary caller JSON, so a request p95 sitting flat at the top of the ladder means the ladder needs changing, not that payloads are exactly that size.\n\nThese histograms count fewer requests than http_requests_total, because a request with no body records no size sample. Do not read their _count series as a request rate.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 23
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_size_bytes_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "request p95"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_response_size_bytes_bucket{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "response p95"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 300,
      "title": "Job Firings",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Firings by Outcome (rate)",
      "description": "submitted, skipped and failed, the three outcomes a firing can have. Read them together: total firings holding steady while submitted falls and skipped rises is not a fault, it is scans taking longer than the interval between them.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "failed"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "skipped"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "submitted"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Firings by Trigger (rate)",
      "description": "schedule is cron firing on its own; manual is somebody pressing the button in the UI or a StartScan call. Scheduled firings should be a regular comb whose spacing matches the cron expressions in use — a flat line at zero while definitions carry schedules means the timers were never rebuilt, which is what a restart looks like here.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (trigger) (rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{trigger}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outcome Share",
      "description": "The same three outcomes as a share of all firings, which is what makes them comparable across a quiet period and a busy one. clamp_min keeps the ratio defined when nothing is firing rather than returning NaN and breaking the stack.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(scalar(sum(rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m]))), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 400,
      "title": "Why Firings Are Skipped or Failed",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Skip Reasons (rate)",
      "description": "definition_already_running is the ordinary one: the previous scan from the same definition had not finished. full_scan_needs_exclusive_access and full_scan_in_progress are a full scan refusing to share with an incremental one in either direction. concurrency_forbidden is a definition configured to never overlap at all. All four are policy, not error — what matters is the trend, because a reason that never clears means a schedule is set faster than its scans take.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "sum"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", outcome=\"skipped\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failure Reasons (rate)",
      "description": "pipeline_unavailable is this service failing to ensure the connector's pipeline before it could submit, so the fault is upstream of the job engine. job_engine_rejected is the engine refusing the submission it was handed. The two point at different services, which is the whole reason the reason label exists.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 41
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "sum"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", outcome=\"failed\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failure Ratio",
      "description": "Failed firings as a share of all firings. Skips are excluded from the numerator on purpose — folding them in would make a correctly throttled schedule look like a broken one.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 41
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.05
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\", outcome=\"failed\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(job_firings_total{job=~\".*datasource-service.*\", namespace=\"$namespace\"}[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "failure ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 500,
      "title": "Per-Pod Drill-Down",
